ons in epileptic encephalopathies. Nature 2013;501:217&#x2013;21.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3773011</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">23934111</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Heinzen EL, Swoboda KJ, Hitomi Y, et al. De novo mutations in ATP1A3 cause alternating hemiplegia of childhood. Nat Genet 2012;44:1030&#x2013;4.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3442240</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">22842232</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Marzin P, Mignot C, Dorison N, et al. Early-onset encephalopathy with paroxysmal movement disorders and epileptic seizures without hemiplegic attacks: About three children with novel ATP1A3 mutations. Brain Dev 2018;40:768&#x2013;74.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">29861155</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Fehr S, Wong K, Chin R, et al. Seizure variables and their relationship to genotype and functional abilities in the CDKL5 disorder. Neurology 2016;87:2206&#x2013;13.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27770071</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kevelam SH, Bierau J, Salvarinova R, et al. Recessive ITPA mutations cause an early infantile encephalopathy. Annals of neurology 2015;78:649&#x2013;58.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26224535</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Piard J, Hawkes L, Milh M, et al. The phenotypic spectrum of WWOX-related disorders: 20 additional cases of WOREE syndrome and review of the literature. Genet Med 2018.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6752669</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30356099</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Veeramah KR, Johnstone L, Karafet TM, et al. Exome sequencing reveals new causal mutations in children with epileptic encephalopathies. Epilepsia 2013;54:1270&#x2013;81.</Citation><ArticleIdList><Article